From: openEuler RISC-V Maintainers <noreply@example.invalid>
Date: Fri, 14 Aug 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] gnulib: normalize unsigned-char localeconv sentinel

License: LGPL-2.1-or-later
Upstream-Status: downstream-only
Origin: openEuler RISC-V package CI

On openEuler's RISC-V build, the C locale's unavailable monetary fields can
be exposed as SCHAR_MAX because the ABI uses an unsigned plain char while the
locale data uses the signed-char sentinel representation.  The bundled
gnulib probe only treated negative values as broken, so configure accepted the
system localeconv implementation and the test suite later rejected the value.

Treat any C-locale frac_digits value other than CHAR_MAX as requiring gnulib's
replacement, and normalize both negative values and SCHAR_MAX in that
replacement.  This preserves the full test suite and the specified CHAR_MAX
interface without changing sed's application code.

Remove this patch when an upstream gnulib release carries equivalent handling
for unsigned-char localeconv sentinels.

---
 configure         | 2 +-
 lib/localeconv.c  | 6 +++---
 m4/localeconv.m4  | 2 +-
 3 files changed, 5 insertions(+), 5 deletions(-)

diff --git a/configure b/configure
--- a/configure
+++ b/configure
@@ -37126,5 +37126,5 @@ else case e in #(
             int main ()
             {
               struct lconv *l = localeconv ();
-              return l->frac_digits != CHAR_MAX && l->frac_digits < 0;
+              return l->frac_digits != CHAR_MAX;
             }
diff --git a/lib/localeconv.c b/lib/localeconv.c
--- a/lib/localeconv.c
+++ b/lib/localeconv.c
@@ -26 +26 @@
-# define FIX_CHAR_VALUE(x) ((x) >= 0 ? (x) : CHAR_MAX)
+# define FIX_CHAR_VALUE(x) ((x) < 0 || (x) == SCHAR_MAX ? CHAR_MAX : (x))
@@ -29 +29 @@
-   members or where fields of type 'char' are set to -1 instead of CHAR_MAX.  */
+   members or where fields of type 'char' are set to a non-CHAR_MAX sentinel.  */
diff --git a/m4/localeconv.m4 b/m4/localeconv.m4
--- a/m4/localeconv.m4
+++ b/m4/localeconv.m4
@@ -27,5 +27,5 @@
             int main ()
             {
               struct lconv *l = localeconv ();
-              return l->frac_digits != CHAR_MAX && l->frac_digits < 0;
+              return l->frac_digits != CHAR_MAX;
             }
